# Project structure

Next.js 15 App Router + TypeScript. Keep layers separated:

| Layer | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Domain | `src/domain/` | Business types and enums — no I/O |
| API | `src/app/api/` | HTTP handlers; Zod in `schema.ts` |
| Data | `src/supabase/` | DB access, mappers, migrations |
| CMS | `src/cms/` | Prismic fetchers and types |
| UI | `src/components/`, `src/app/` | React components and pages |
| Shared | `src/lib/` | Utilities, logger, SEO helpers |

## Conventions

- Import domain types from `@/domain/*`; do not duplicate enums in API or UI
- DB row shapes stay in `src/supabase/`; map to domain types via mappers
- Use `@/lib/logger` (`logError`, `logInfo`, `LogModule`) — never raw `console.*` outside `logger.ts`
- Path alias: `@/` → `src/`
- README-* files document integrations (Supabase, Prismic, Auth, Sentry)

## Admin

- Legacy admin: `src/app/admin/`
- Admin v2 (in progress): `src/app/admin/v2/` + `src/components/admin-v2/`
